          "@type": "Answer",
          text: "Japanese logic puzzles are grid based puzzles that can be solved entirely through pure reasoning, with no vocabulary, trivia, or guessing required. Most were popularized by the Japanese puzzle publisher Nikoli. Famous examples include Sudoku, Shikaku, Akari, Kakuro, Nonograms, Slitherlink, and Hashiwokakero. Each puzzle uses one simple rule set, and every well made puzzle has exactly one solution that can be reached by logic alone."
